b'MUMBAI: India captain Virat Kohli isn't known to indulge in hyperbole.


So, when he labelled Jasprit Bumrah the 'best bowler in the world' and someone he 'wouldn't want to face' on a spicy pitch like Perth, following India's momentous Test win over Australia at the MCG on Sunday, it more than stressed where the Gujarat fast bowler stood in the eyes of his teammates starting from the captain.


