Excerpts:


Are you comfortable with the perception that there is a huge difference in quality between your serve and other strokes...

Jeez! I mean unless you feel that way \xe2\x80\xa6 You cannot have the results I have had or get to where I am without having a complete game. If you have any weaknesses, people are going to expose that. I really feel that I have an all court game, I have worked hard on all the different aspects of my game.


You must have expected to play the Wimbledon quarterfinal against Federer on the Centre Court...

Yes. There is a lot of silly politics involved \xe2\x80\xa6 who is going to be playing where? I heard Federer was upset (for playing on court No. 1). It was kind of interesting. Those guys are more often than not playing on the same court match after match. I had played on Court 1 against Monfils, so I was a little used to that. I didn't feel too bad for Federer that he had to adapt because I have to do that pretty much every single tournament.


There was also the issue with day and night matches in Australia\xe2\x80\xa6

I just feel that the champion he (Federer) is, even if he had to play day matches, he would have adjusted and found a way. Every player has the right to make scheduling request. Obviously if Roger asks the tournament is going to take it seriously. He is so popular and every tournament wants him in the final. It's not his fault.


Isn't the World Team Cup in conflict with the Davis Cup?

World Team Cup has been in existence before. Speaking in the last two years in the ATP, we felt that we had a great opportunity to have a team event to start our year off. There was a lot of frustration from the ITF, but \xe2\x80\xa6 they have not been very accommodating. At the end of the day, they do their own thing. All we can do is control our own tour.


Wimbledon has introduced tie-break at 12-all in the deciding set\xe2\x80\xa6

It is good to see some kind of end point. I would have liked to have it at 6-all like a regular set. Probably, they wanted to distinguish it. 12-all can still get very long. You are basically playing six sets.


Would you favour the super tie-break of Australian Open?

It is slightly better, Australia could have kept it to normal tie-break instead of super tie-break. Now we have four Grand Slams with four different formats for a single event.


How do you deal with defeats in Grand Slam finals?

It's always tough. You put a lot into it. I feel for the most part it is about perspective. At the end of the day, the world is not going to end. It is just a tennis match. I will be more disappointed if I don't perform well.


If not for Roger, Rafa and Novak, could others have won more majors?

The three of them have won 50 Grand Slams. Their dominance has been unmatched. If they had not been around there would have been more Grand Slam winners, but at the same time tennis wouldn't have been the same sport that it is today.


Do you feel unlucky to be playing when these three are around?

No! It has been a great experience to be able to compete with these guys. It would be stupid to think of any other reality, because that is what the reality is. I have to accept the challenge and I have to figure out a way to beat these guys.

'

