b'Coimbatore: The liquidity deficit in the banking system widened to an over two-year high in the week ended December 28 despite the RBI infusing liquidity to the tune of Rs 15,000 crore. It was the 12th consecutive week (since October 9, 2018) wherein the banking system has faced an overall liquidity deficit.

The average liquidity deficit, at Rs 1,58,517 crore, for the week ended December 28 was higher than the average liquidity deficit of Rs 1,49,635 crore during the previous week. 



