b'Mumbai: Life Insurance Corporation (LIC), the country\xe2\x80\x99s largest financial institution, is without a full-time chairman following the retirement of V K Sharma on December 31. While the corporation\xe2\x80\x99s managing director Hemant Bhargava will be holding charge as chairman, a Banks Board Bureau (BBB) panel has started the interview process for eligible candidates.

Given that Bhargava and the other two managing directors are due to retire in 2019, the BBB panel will be interviewing executive directors for the top job. Among the MDs, Sunita Sharma is scheduled to retire in March, B Venugopal in May, and Bhargava in July. Another MD position fell vacant after Usha Sangwan retired in September 2018.



