            According to reports, eight candidates are in the fray for the two positions of chairman and managing director \xe2\x80\x94 ED (personnel) Mukesh Kumar Gupta, ED (customer relationship) K Ganesh, ED S Nallakuttalam and LICMF CEO Raj Kumar, along with zonal managers M R Kumar (Delhi), H S Shashi Kumar (Bhopal), T C Susheel Kumar (Hyderabad) and Vipin Anand (Mumbai).

The BBB will interview the eligible candidates and send its recommendations to the Appointments Committee of the Cabinet headed by the Prime Minister. The government will then name the candidate after getting all the required clearances. This is the first time that the BBB is conducting the interview for the top position in LIC. In the past, interviews were conducted by a finance ministry panel with a top official of the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDAI) present too.

