b'SYDNEY: It is not often that an Australian team carries the tag of an \xe2\x80\x98underdog\xe2\x80\x99 while playing at home \xe2\x80\x94 especially going into a game at the historic Sydney Cricket Ground (SCG), where they haven\xe2\x80\x99t lost a Test match in the last eight years.


England were the last team to humble Australia at the SCG, back in 2011. This is a venue where the hosts have since won five Tests and drawn two. Australia, who boast a win percentage of 55.66 at this venue, have won 59 of the 106 Tests they have played here, drawn 19 and lost 28. But then, these are difficult times for Australian cricket. 


