Later in the afternoon, Australian prime minister Scott Morrison hosted the members of both teams at his residence in Kirribilli. Morrison presented a memento to each of the two captains, following which both Virat Kohli and Paine addressed the guests briefly.

Kohli, who was accompanied by his wife Anushka, highlighted the growing importance of cricketing exchanges between the two countries and maintained that playing Australia in their own backward remains the biggest challenge for any team.

Kohli, however, said that Team India are not under pressure even though they are on the cusp of winning their maiden Test series on Australian soil. Adding that it\xe2\x80\x99s a historic occasion for both the teams because of the way the series is placed, Kohli said he and his team were looking forward to the final Test.

The Indian captain, who ushered in the New Year on Monday night, also tweeted a picture of himself and Anushka in front of the Sydney Opera House. Several Indian players and their wives also braved inclement weather to catch the festivities and the fireworks display at the Sydney Harbour Bridge at midnight.

'

