b'New Delhi: Crisis-ridden Jet Airways has defaulted on loan repayment to banks, following which its credit rating has been downgraded. In a statement to BSE, the airline late on Tuesday said: \xe2\x80\x9cPayment of interest and principal instalment due to the consortium of Indian Banks (led by State Bank of India) on December 31, 2018, has been delayed due to temporary cashflow mismatch and the company has engaged with them in relation to the same.\xe2\x80\x9d 

The Jet scrip closed 6.2% lower at Rs 263.75 on BSE Wednesday.



