b'NEW DELHI: A parliamentary panel has recommended setting up of a committee to evaluate the role, powers and authority of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and has said it expects the central bank to provide a coherent road map for 11 public sector banks (PSBs) to come out of its prompt corrective action (PCA).


\xe2\x80\x9cThe committee would thus recommend that the government should constitute a high-powered committee to evaluate the role, powers and authority of the RBI in its entirety, while also appraising the economic impact of the various NPA resolution guidelines/schemes formulated by the RBI from time to time,\xe2\x80\x9d the parliamentary standing committee on finance, headed by Congress leader Veerappa Moily, said in its report tabled in Parliament on Thursday.


