b'Chennai-headquartered Samunnati Financial Intermediation and Services, an NBFC focused on lending to farmers and agriculture entities, has raised $5 million in debt by issue of Non-Convertible Debentures to Dutch development bank FMO, an impact investor. The investment was facilitated through MASSIF, a Dutch government fund managed by FMO. Samunnati will utilise the funds to extend their support to small-holder farmer organisations and agri-enterprises by financing their working capital needs. Samunnati\xe2\x80\x99s existing investors include Swiss impact investor responsAbility, PE firms Elevar Equity and Accel Partners. The NBFC has disbursed over Rs 1,400 crore worth of credit till date, and claims to have impacted 2 million farmers, indirectly, across 14 states. The lender primarily deals with two customer segments- that of community-based organizations in the agri space, and agri-based enterprises being the other.

