\xe2\x80\x9cThe business plan is to build even as we are repairing,\xe2\x80\x9d said Mahapatra \xe2\x80\x94 who took charge in September 2018 after a career in SBI. As part of this mission, the bank has created a new stressed asset vertical. \xe2\x80\x9cWhat is unique about this is that while the government mandate is to refer loans above Rs 50 crore to the stressed asset vertical, we have decided to refer all loans above Rs 5 crore,\xe2\x80\x9d said Mahapatra. As a result, all troubled loans above this figure will be referred from the branch to the head office directly without having to go to the zonal or regional offices.

To boost lending to small businesses, the bank has taken two new initiatives. First, it is tying up with fintechs to distribute loans. It has already tied up with Atyati Technologies, a fintech with a technology platform \xe2\x80\x98GANASEVA\xe2\x80\x99 to provide loans to hitherto uncovered medium and small enterprises for up to Rs 10 lakh. It has also tied up with SREI Equipment Finance, which has a lion\xe2\x80\x99s share of the infrastructure equipment finance market in India. Under the partnership SREI will originate loans for Syndicate Bank. \xe2\x80\x9cOur approach is to go for partnership wherever we do not have the capability,\xe2\x80\x9d said Mahapatra.

