b'NEW DELHI: The government has ordered a clampdown on shipments from Chinese e-commerce platforms allegedly sent to India under the guise of gifts. This will tighten the noose around e-tailers that exploit loopholes in regulations. The move by the customs department to impose curbs on such consignments comes against the backdrop of the government receiving several complaints about sellers on Chinese online platforms, including Shein, Club Factory and AliExpress, sending goods as \xe2\x80\x98gifts\xe2\x80\x99 to customers in India to avoid duties.


This brings the prices of such goods down and gives them an unfair advantage over sellers on domestic e-commerce marketplaces. The government is expected to take up the issue in the draft e-commerce policy that is set to be unveiled soon. Officials said the clampdown will also have an impact on illegal food products and spurious cosmetics being smuggled into India.


