b'SYDNEY: Cheteshwar Pujara once again put mind over matter and defied Australian bowlers all day to notch up his 18th century as India ended the opening day of the final Test comfortably placed at 303 for 4 after skipper Virat Kohli won the toss and elected to bat.


Pujara, who walked into bat in the second over of the day, was unbeaten on 130 \xe2\x80\x94 his third hundred of the series. Keeping him company was Hanuma Vihari on 39 when stumps were drawn.


