Last month, Apple was also granted a major patent for smart fabrics that integrates smart fabrics with integrated circuity and force sensors, making it possible to have sensors like blood pressure monitors embedded. "The glove finger may include fabric that has been woven, knit, braided and/or sewn to form a shape appropriate for receiving a user's finger. When the user presses glove finger in downwards towards a desk surface, a compressive force will be applied to the fabric and the force sensors between the finger and a surface will be able to take readings sent to an external Apple device," the patent reads.

