He pointed out that in AP, the bank has been reporting a robust growth in the home as well as agriculture loans segments. \xe2\x80\x9cThe growth in home loans in AP was highest in the country among all circles in the last financial year as well as this fiscal till November. Vijayawada and Visakhapatnam stand at first and ninth spot, respectively, in the percentage growth in SBI\xe2\x80\x99s home loans in the entire country,\xe2\x80\x9d he said, adding that this fiscal till December 19, its home loans portfolio grew by Rs 3,398 crore in AP.

He pointed out that the robust growth in home loans segment in AP was not a new phenomenon for SBI as traditionally this region has always been clocking impressive numbers. He explained that in other SBI circles, the business growth is generally driven by one to two cities, whereas in AP, around 10 to 12 centres such as Vizag, Rajahmundry, Kurnool and Guntur, among others contribute to the overall growth. 

\xe2\x80\x9cWe have a widespread market due to which the volume growth is high across the state,\xe2\x80\x9d he said, adding that in AP, the home loan segment has been growing by around 20% in the last three years and even before bifurcation, it was showing similar growth. In AP, SBI has around 40% share in the home loan segment.

The bank has been allocated 2 acres land in the capital city for its office, for which it will be seeking all the requisite clearances from its head office next fiscal.


