b'NEW DELHI: Swedish telecom equipment major Ericsson has petitioned the Supreme Court to arrest Reliance Communications (RCom) chief Anil Ambani over recurring delays in payment of its dues worth Rs 550 crore, and has accused the embattled businessman of engaging in \xe2\x80\x9cgross and wilful contempt\xe2\x80\x9d of the apex court. The company has said that insolvency proceedings should be initiated against RCom and its spectrum & tower sale deal with Reliance Jio should be stopped \xe2\x80\x9cwith immediate effect\xe2\x80\x9d.


In a fresh petition submitted before the top court, Ericsson alleged that the delays in payment by Anil and his companies have been \xe2\x80\x9cwilful, contumacious and persistent\xe2\x80\x9d. \xe2\x80\x9cThe respondents have abused the process of law to the hilt and caused grave damage to the interest of justice\xe2\x80\xa6 having committed and guilty of contempt of court, be directed to be detained in civil prison unless\xe2\x80\xa6 (they) purge themselves by making payment of Rs 550 crore along with interest,\xe2\x80\x9d Ericsson\xe2\x80\x99s petition states.


