Throwing light on some of the trends would be Mukesh Ambani, Paul Polman, Amitabh Bachchan, Andre Agassi and Piyush Pandey, to name a few. What\xe2\x80\x99s more, social humanoid \xe2\x80\x98Sophia\xe2\x80\x99 has also been listed as a speaker.

In the digital age, where brand continues to be a religion, the theme of the 44th edition of the IAA World Congress \xe2\x80\x94 \xe2\x80\x98Brand Dharma\xe2\x80\x99 \xe2\x80\x94 aims to bring to life the basic principles that a brand has to follow to connect with its customers and society at large. IAA chairman & world president Srinivasan K Swamy, who is also CMD of R K Swamy BBDO, said, \xe2\x80\x9cToday\xe2\x80\x99s brand has to stand for what is righteous. Dharma is an Indian/Sanskrit word that stands for doing one\xe2\x80\x99s duty, do what is right for consumers, society at large and must stand for a cause. It is a whole new world today where products and services will have to not only satisfy consumers on quality and delivery, but they should stand for a higher purpose.\xe2\x80\x9d

IAA is known for its support to freedom of commercial speech and has been at the forefront of promoting self-regulation in advertising. Hindustan Unilever CMD Sanjiv Mehta, who is a member of the governing council, said, \xe2\x80\x9cThe IAA World Congress is coming to India at a very opportune time. It is a forum where some of the foremost thinkers of our generation will set the ground for future standards of advertising and marketing based on purpose and ethics and where tech is a force for good.\xe2\x80\x9d

The World Congress is expected to go beyond marketing. Madison World CMD Sam Balsara said, \xe2\x80\x9cIt\xe2\x80\x99ll cover the business of business and not just the business of marketing. One of the things that worries people is what\xe2\x80\x99s going to happen tomorrow? How do I prepare my organisation for tomorrow? There will be tremendous learning and eye-opening exposure on this front.\xe2\x80\x9d

Given the multiple challenges faced by the industry today, the event is expected to address a crucial question on every leader\xe2\x80\x99s lips \xe2\x80\x94 \xe2\x80\x98What\xe2\x80\x99s coming next?\xe2\x80\x99 Swamy said, \xe2\x80\x9cWe live in interesting times, where tomorrow is here already for some, and tomorrow will come for some, a day later.\xe2\x80\x9d He added, \xe2\x80\x9cOn the one hand, we have consumers who are constantly multi-tasking with serious attention deficit. And on the other, we are overwhelmed by media choices. On top of this, there are changes caused by technology and newer platforms for reviewing content, either for education or entertainment. The various speakers at the Congress will address many of these issues and would offer some clues as to how to stay ahead in this complex and ever evolving mar-com (marketing communications) space.\xe2\x80\x9d

Lodestar UM India CEO Nandini Dias said \xe2\x80\x98Brand Dharma\xe2\x80\x99 will spark a global dialogue to review principles, global institutional framework, account-based content marketing, trusted user-generated content, chat-based artificial intelligence, automated ad tech and audience analytics. Collectively, these transformations are changing how individuals and companies relate to each other and the world at large. \xe2\x80\x9cWe hope that the marketing and communication industry acknowledges these changes and adapts and works together to create new opportunities,\xe2\x80\x9d said Dias.

Another significant fact about the 44th World Congress is that it is taking place in India when IAA is headed by its first Indian chairman & world president. \xe2\x80\x9cIndia is the flavour of the world today and it has a good reputation for handling global conferences with jazz and great content,\xe2\x80\x9d said Balsara. Headquartered in New York, IAA is present in 55 countries through chapters and various educational institutions.


IAA meet expected to go beyond marketing

