From there, he went from strength to strength and brought the Australian bowlers to their knees. His series aggregate now stands at 350 \xe2\x80\x94 the most by an Indian glovesman in Australia, eclipsing Syed Kirmani\xe2\x80\x99s 305 in the five-match series in 1977-78. Pant also surpassed Virat Kohli\xe2\x80\x99s tally (282) to become the secondhighest run-scorer for India in this series behind the prolific Pujara (521).

