Not a catastrophe, but certainly cause for concern for team Djokovic as the Serb heads Down Under for the opening Grand Slam of the year, the Australian Open.In Friday\xe2\x80\x99s late-evening semifinals at the picture perfect Khalifa International Complex, Djokovic\xe2\x80\x99s challenge, which appeared well on course for a setand-a-half, came apart at the wheels as he crashed to a 6-3, 6-7 (6-8), 4-6 loss in 2 hours and 35-minutes.

