b'Chennai NBFC Northern Arc Capital closed a persistent securitization transaction on Monday, structuring a product for EssKay Fincorp to raise Rs 38 crore in debt. The underlying assets securitized in the transaction are vehicle loans of EssKay Fincorp Limited. Northern Arc (erstwhile, IFMR Capital), which executed a similar product in 2011 for micro finance loans, said the current transaction is the first-of-its-kind post the issuance of the Securitisation Guidelines in 2012. A persistent securitization structure allows the originator entity to raise longer-term funding using shorter tenor assets. The collections from the initial pool of underlying loans are utilised to buy new pools of loans over the course of a pre-determined duration called replenishment period. In case of Esskay Fincorp, the replenishment period is determined as six months, during which additional loans will be purchased on a quarterly basis. \xe2\x80\x9cThis increases the quantum of funding that Esskay is expected to receive by 50%,\xe2\x80\x9d Northern Arc Capital said in a statement.\xe2\x80\x9cWe believe it [the transaction has great potential given the credit profile and asset quality of many of our partners that will provide investors the confidence to stay invested in their transactions for a longer period of time,\xe2\x80\x9d Kshama Fernandes, CEO, Northern Arc Capital said.

