December is typically a low wholesale month for the passenger vehicle and two wheeler industry and tyre wear and tear is also less in winter. So inventories tend to be high, he added.

Crude prices have come down from $86 to $54 therefore products like synthetic rubber, carbon black etc are all cheaper now. 

Natural rubber prices are also down from Rs 135 per kg mid last year to Rs 115-120 per kg right now, said Singh.

\xe2\x80\x9cThe adverse effects of the increase in crude, interest rates, depreciation of INR and lack of festive demand uptick has been the maximum in the third quarter. There is some comfort that the rupee has not weakened further and crude prices have softened over the last two months. This is a welcome change for the industry. We also expect demand to resume to normal levels in the near term. A decision to lower price or not is subject to competitive pressures and will be taken on a case to case basis,\xe2\x80\x9d said Anant Goenka, managing director, CEAT.


