Prior to Maezawa, the most retweeted message on Twitter was created back in 2017 by Carter Wilkerson from US who was then 16 years old. In his tweet, he had asked how many retweets were needed to receive 365 days of free nuggets from Wendy's. The fast food restaurant had responded that about "18 million" retweets were required. 

While Wilkerson has not reached the initial goal of 18 million, he has achieved the record for "Most retweeted message on Twitter" - formerly held by @TheEllenShow's Ellen DeGeneres and her iconic Oscars selfie, the Guinness World Records said on its website. And while he could not get the 18 million, but since Wilkerson broke the record, the fast food chain Wendy's agreed to give him a year's worth of free nuggets. 

Now that Yusaku Maezawa has won the title of posting the most-retweeted tweet, we will have to wait and see how the distribution of wealth pans out amongst his followers. The 43-year-old Yusaku Maezawa has a net-worth of $2.7 billion, according to Forbes.

