b'MUMBAI: When Rupayan Roy was being wheeled in for heart transplant surgery, several thoughts ran through his mind. His two-and-a-half-year-old son was fast asleep, blissfully unaware of the turmoil, even as Rupayan wondered if he would see his child again. His wife, Jayati, was in tears. 


But that was in July, 2016. Today, almost three years later, Rupayan, an LIC HR manager, is running marathons. He will be participating in his first Tata Mumbai Marathon in the city on January 20. It will be his fourth run of over 20km in a little over a year.


