\xe2\x80\x9cA root cause analysis on the A320Neo issues was carried out. In-flight engine shutdown cases in India was found to be lower than the global benchmark,\xe2\x80\x99\xe2\x80\x99 said a source adding that there were higher number of such incidents in India because two Indian carriers were among the largest clients of these engines. 

\xe2\x80\x9cThe number of incidents on A320Neos per thousand hours of flying in India is low,\xe2\x80\x9d the source said adding that the ministry was satisfied with the corrective action taken by the airlines and Pratt and Whitney.

