Hockey India took the decision when they received two separate teams from as many factions of VHA for the 9th Hockey India National Championship 2019 to be held in Chennai on Wednesday.

A faction led by allegedly suspended VHA president BC Bhartia had sent the Vidarbha team to Chennai on Monday. The Hockey India was in favour of Bhartia\xe2\x80\x99s faction and had made up their mind to let them play the national tournament. Bhartia\xe2\x80\x99s squad was even welcomed and was given accommodation from Monday morning in Chennai.

However, another VHA faction led by one of the vice presidents Arvind Joshi, selected Vidarbha team, claiming their move as constitutionally correct. Joshi-led executive committee had suspended Bhartia and secretary Vinod Gavai for their autocratic behavior in December and reported the same to Hockey India.

The Joshi-led faction took the approval of executive committee as mentioned in VHA constitution, which Bhartia and Gavai did not take, and forwarded the selected team to Hockey India on Monday evening.

As soon as Hockey India received the second squad from VHA, Hockey India president Md. Mushtaque Ahmad and secretary general Rajinder Singh suspended VHA\xe2\x80\x99s associate membership and seized their entry from for all the national championships to be played in the 2019 season.

After the suspension, Hockey Tamil Nadu unit, the organizers in Chennai, asked the Vidarbha squad to leave their accommodation facility at 11 am on Tuesday.

The entire saga of controversies started after Bhartia and Gavai ran the association on their own term without taking elected executive committee into confidence. The affairs got murkier when Gavai went on to give affiliation to two clubs in Wardha district. Then, he allotted inter-district tournament to the affiliated unit in Chandrapur without VHA\xe2\x80\x99s executive committee approval.

When the Chandrapur unit denied holding the tournament without VHA\xe2\x80\x99s executive body approval, Gavai shifted the meet to Wardha in haste, where as many as five out of six affiliated districts backed out calling it an illegal tournament and claimed players were at loss. The executive body approval is mandatory for all inter-district tournaments of all sports considering sports quota jobs in government sector.

