b'Indian cos reaffirm their faith in domestic M&As to gain quick traction as it gets tougher to go greenfield. Moreover, t
he new bankruptcy law has provided prospective players an opportunity to bid swiftly for failing cos

M&A is a strategic capability that can give companies an edge that their peers will struggle to replicate\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x80\x94 this is a rationale that Indian firms have bought into fully only in the last few years. Till a decade ago, the argument for \xe2\x80\x98build versus buy\xe2\x80\x99 in the domestic context would always have the same outcome \xe2\x80\x94 go greenfield. The idea of paying a multiple to earnings for taking a competitor out of business was unthinkable as the argument was that the same plant/facility can be built in 24-36 months at five times lower value.


