b'MUMBAI: Despite his superb show with the bat in Australia, where he rounded off a successful tour with an unbeaten 159 in the final Test, Rishabh Pant hasn't been included in India's ODI side for the three games against Australia and the five matches against New Zealand thereafter.


The selectors have chosen to play him in the five ODIs at home against the England Lions instead, but voices are now growing that a superb stroke-player like him has to be an integral part of the Indian team for all the three formats of the game. On Wednesday evening at the Legends' Club function at the Cricket Club of India (CCI) to celebrate legendary all-rounder Kapil Dev's 60th birthday, former India wicket-keeper Farokh Engineer made a pertinent point in this regard.


                    (function(){
                      var adContainer = '<div id="div-gpt-ad-1485328452682222244" data-size="fluid" data-adsslot="TOI/TOI_ROS/TOI_ROS_AS/TOI_ROS_AS_Mrec_MID_300" class="webonly alC"></div>';
