            A Kotak study comparing retail data for FY18 and FY17 shows that the top 5 metro markets \xe2\x80\x94 Delhi, Mumbai (including Navi Mumbai), Bengaluru, Chennai and Pune \xe2\x80\x94 saw a 7% fall in retail sales in FY18 compared to FY17. 

However, rest of India grew by over 12%. 

Given that the real volumes depend substantially on these creamy layer metro markets, the concentration of dealerships has been in these geographies as well.

\xe2\x80\x9cDealerships are facing considerable amount of stress due to the demand drop in passenger vehicle market which also came with renewed aggression from auto companies to push extra stocks and increase their network footprint,\xe2\x80\x9d said a senior official from one of the top three auto financing firms. \xe2\x80\x9cIn Mumbai for instance, there are four dealerships of a mass market car brand which have shut down in the past one year.\xe2\x80\x9d Each of these dealerships owe upwards of Rs 50 crore to banks.

Nor is this restricted to price sensitive mass market brands alone. Even luxury brands are facing a similar scenario. For instance, in Chennai, Mercedes Benz dealership Transcar has shut down last week after 21 years in the business. Sources say a host of reasons have made it difficult for even high-margin luxury car dealerships to make money. For one, luxe brands insist on high infrastructure spend. Also, most brands are now going for multiple dealerships in cherry markets like the top five geographies which affects profitability. Finally, in a slow sales market, discounts drive stocks. \xe2\x80\x9cMost companies, including luxury brands, have lost the power of pricing and high discounting is eating into dealer margins, affecting viability,\xe2\x80\x9d said a car dealer.

Car companies, for their part, say the dealer attrition is part of the normal ups and downs of business and dealers should be able to handle it if their financial health is not compromised. Said Pawan Goenka, MD, M&M: \xe2\x80\x9cUps and downs are part of a business cycle and only those dealers will have a problem handling it that are financially unsound.\xe2\x80\x9d 

Agreed Saharsh Damani, chief executive officer of the Federation of Automobile Dealers Association (FADA), \xe2\x80\x9cJust one bad year will not make a dealership unviable and those that are shutting down must have other financial issues.\xe2\x80\x9d Others like Hyundai maintain that the company, though aggressive, is trying to hand hold its dealers through this turbulence. \xe2\x80\x9cWe are helping our dealers by offering them larger stocks of the best-selling Creta for instance. We are aggressive but not at the cost of business viability,\xe2\x80\x9d said a Hyundai spokesman.

Dealer sources, for their part, admit some promoters do divert money to other businesses causing financial instability. But pressure on margins due to high investment demands, multiple dealerships in metro markets, aggressive wholesale billing and high discounting is a deadly combination in a sluggish market. \xe2\x80\x9cHaving high discounts and multiple touch points is very good for the consumer but bad for the dealer business,\xe2\x80\x9d said another car dealer. \xe2\x80\x9cThat includes expansion into non-metro/hinterland markets.\xe2\x80\x9d 

Dealers also say some of their pain is structural. \xe2\x80\x9cEarlier the financing margin was 2.5-3% which is now down to 0.7%,\xe2\x80\x9d said a Bengaluru-based car dealer. \xe2\x80\x9cAlso there has been a 20% increase in working capital requirements due to GST.\xe2\x80\x9d Sluggish sales means inventory is up from 45 days to 3-4 months. "For a segment that employs around 1.5 lakh people per state, this unviability is not good news," he said.


