 organized a human chain on January 3, he added. The workers, he said, have not got their increments and bonus which is pending till the wage settlement.The management, for its part, maintained that it only recognizes UUHE as it has majority support and does not have any political affiliation. \xe2\x80\x9cThe wage negotiations are a routine process and happen once every 3 years and it is at a fairly advanced stage,\xe2\x80\x9d said a senior management official. \xe2\x80\x9cThe negotiations should close by February and everything, including bonus and increments, will be decided through the settlement,\xe2\x80\x9d he added. When contacted, a HMI spokesperson said that the company\xe2\x80\x99s \xe2\x80\x9cproduction is on schedule\xe2\x80\x9d and its \xe2\x80\x9cwage negotiations with the recognized union is an advanced stage of discussion and is progressing smoothly\xe2\x80\x9d.Management sources say the question of disclosure is up to UUHE and the fact that it has maximum membership is corroborated by data because the union fees are directly deducted from the salary. HMIEU officials say it won most of the posts in the cooperative society election last year which shows it has substantial support among employees. HMI has seen strikes and labour turbulence four times in the last 10 years. The company \xe2\x80\x94 the second largest car company in domestic sales and the largest exporter \xe2\x80\x94 has around 2,200 permanent employees. HMIEU supporters say there are also nearly 5,000 trainees who are working on the assembly line although there are no temporary staff. HMI officials say the numbers are not that high and the company accepts apprentices who are then trained \xe2\x80\x9cas per law\xe2\x80\x9d and as mandated by the government.'

b'MUMBAI: India has emerged as the biggest hiring market outside the US for the world\xe2\x80\x99s largest financial services technology provider \xe2\x80\x94 FIS. The company has recruited over 14,000 professionals in India across cities, up from 8,000 in 2015, and the headcount continues to grow.


FIS had entered India nearly two decades ago by helping banks set up the first ATM network. Since then, it has moved on to providing core banking and other technology solutions, besides managing ATMs. 


