\xe2\x80\x9cATM was the tip of the spear for us. It is what brought us into the country,\xe2\x80\x9d said FIS chairman, president and CEO Gary Norcross. While the number of machines in India has showed signs of plateauing, Norcross believes this will continue to be a growing business as many ATMs are due for replacement.




Even if ATM deployments slow down, Norcross is not worried. \xe2\x80\x9cWe look at business holistically. If one of our product lines is contracting, we make sure that we have a solution to take advantage of where our clients are spending money,\xe2\x80\x9d he said. 

Norcross is in India to take advantage of tech spending in the next big wave globally \xe2\x80\x94 open banking and in digital banking. FIS is offering banks its new Digital One platform, which enables omni-channel banking based on an open architecture. The software allows banks to offer digital solutions for both assisted and unassisted channels.

Norcross cautions banks against depending too much on partnerships with fintechs. \xe2\x80\x9cInstitutions need to be careful because they need to be regulatory compliant and meet requirements of the industry. What you don\xe2\x80\x99t want to do is embrace a small startup that cannot meet the burden of regulatory compliance,\xe2\x80\x9d said Norcross. He suggests that banks leave the fintech partnering to FIS. \xe2\x80\x9cWith FIS, you get a Fortune 500 company that understands regulatory framework very well, and also brings disruption and takes responsibility for all of the oversight that goes with them,\xe2\x80\x9d he added.

According to Norcross, just like the core-banking solution helped level the playing field across banks, FIS\xe2\x80\x99 cloud-based solutions can enable the smallest banks offer digital banking at low costs. \xe2\x80\x9cIn some countries, we not only roll out digital framework, we roll it out in our own private cloud that allows financial institutions to leapfrog and drive digital capabilities at a lower cost,\xe2\x80\x9d said Norcross.

He added that some public sector banks were behind in digital and in certain areas of automation. Also, they would need to look at their enterprise fraud risk management capability. Norcross expects FIS\xe2\x80\x99 growth rate in India to be faster than the rate of GDP growth. In India, the company has centres of excellence in Chandigarh, Gurgaon, Noida, Mumbai, Pune, Bengaluru and Chennai. \xe2\x80\x9cWe are pleased with the level of talent we are getting out of this country and the tenure we are building here. A lot of our employees are becoming long-tenure associates of FIS,\xe2\x80\x9d he said. India became the biggest hiring ground this month after FIS exited a joint venture in Brazil.


