Grover Zampa (originally Grover Vineyards) was founded by Kanwal Grover in 1988. In 2012, it was merged with Vallee de Vin (owner of the Zampa brand) to form the current corporate entity. After the acquisitions of Four Seasons and Charosa, the Grovers\xe2\x80\x99 stake will come down to 6% from 11%, while Viswanathan\xe2\x80\x99s will increase from 50% to 69%. Other investors \xe2\x80\x94 Quintela, AVT Group (known for its tea play) and original promoters of Vallee de Vin \xe2\x80\x94 will continue to hold 9%, 10% and 6% in the winemaker.

