The matter pertains to Pandya and Rahul\xe2\x80\x99s comments on filmmaker Karan Johar\xe2\x80\x99s show Koffee With Karan that was streamed four days ago. The comments have largely been deemed \xe2\x80\x94 in the mainstream and social media \xe2\x80\x94 as \xe2\x80\x9ccringeworthy\xe2\x80\x9d and \xe2\x80\x9cdisgusting\xe2\x80\x9d. Insiders say \xe2\x80\x9cThis is not a legal issue at all. This is about BCCI\xe2\x80\x99s own Code of Conduct for cricketers. This is simply waste of time.\xe2\x80\x9d

Clause 17 & 18 of the BCCI\xe2\x80\x99s constitution, although, call for either the Apex Council or an ombudsman to intervene in such matters.

Kohli and Shastri, are meanwhile kept waiting. Until a reply comes in writing from BCCI\xe2\x80\x99s legal team, the CoA is in no position to take any action. The Board\xe2\x80\x99s inability to take the call stems from a series of e-mails that have been exchanged between members of the CoA and Edulji\xe2\x80\x99s refusal to agree with CoA chairman Vinod Rai on all matters concerning BCCI. Below is a trail of e-mails \xe2\x80\x94 in possession of TOI \xe2\x80\x94 that present a detailed scenario of what transpired.

On Wednesday, January 9, at 10.38am, hours after Twitter had feasted on Pandya and Rahul\xe2\x80\x99s talk show with Johar, BCCI CEO Rahul Johri wrote an e-mail to Rai and Edulji, stating: \xe2\x80\x9cIt is been brought to our notice that (Hardik Pandya & KL Rahul) made a few statements which have not been well received in the media. We would suggest that a notice be sent seeking explanation within 24 hours. Please advise.\xe2\x80\x9d

To this, Rai replied at 11.26 am and said: \xe2\x80\x9cOnly within 24 hours\xe2\x80\x9d.

At 11.29 am, Edulji replied to both stating (verbatim): \xe2\x80\x9cStrict action should be taken against both as they can\xe2\x80\x99t speak about women in such a manner. They should be banned for a match or two to show we respect women and won\xe2\x80\x99t allow players to be disrespectful\xe2\x80\x9d.

To this, Rai replied an hour later, insisting notices should be sent, and said: \xe2\x80\x9cSend the notice. We can decide the action today\xe2\x80\x9d.

Pandya then went on to tweet an apology before drafting his reply to the showcause notice, reported by TOI on Thursday. Rahul sent a separate e-mail.

\xe2\x80\x98Apology doesn\xe2\x80\x99t appear sincere\xe2\x80\x99

Soon after receiving the replies, Rai wrote to Edulji and Johri, saying: \xe2\x80\x9cThe apology has obviously been drafted by the agency. Doesn\xe2\x80\x99t appear sincere. I am inclined to suggest a penalty. But since I have not seen the clip, maybe Diana would like to suggest some penalty. There should be a penalty? What do you feel? Could be different for both players depending upon what they have said in the show\xe2\x80\x9d.

Sources say his views were based on the logic that Rahul remained relatively guarded while Pandya did most of the talking.

Rai then went through the excerpts of what was spoken on Johar\xe2\x80\x99s show and replied again: \xe2\x80\x9cI have seen the remarks made by these two players on the show in print today. Very crass. No apology can cover it. I had asked Diana to suggest a penalty because I had not seen the clip. I think we need to give both of them a two-match suspension. If Diana agrees, Rahul please draft an appropriate instruction and issue today as their explanations have come in. Separately please prepare an advisory to all BCCI contracted players and support staff \xe2\x80\x9d.

However, Edulji, who had earlier advised the two-match ban, retracted from her earlier statement and instead wrote back to Rai and Johri, saying: \xe2\x80\x9cThe (BCCI) secretary and legal (Amarchand Mangaldas) may kindly opine\xe2\x80\x9d.

Sources say BCCI\xe2\x80\x99s legal team Amarchand Mangaldas is clear that this is not a legal matter but one that involves the BCCI\xe2\x80\x99s own Code of Conduct.

Board secretary Amitabh Choudhary says: \xe2\x80\x9cSuspension must happen immediately\xe2\x80\x9d. BCCI\xe2\x80\x99s acting president CK Khanna wrote: \xe2\x80\x9cComments are crass and highly irresponsible. I suggest strict action\xe2\x80\x9d.

'

