b'Chennia: A rating mechanism for fintech startups can make it easier for them to source business from large banks and financial institutions, government and other industry officials said on Friday. Putting forward a proposal to devise a ranking system for the country\xe2\x80\x99s fintech enterprises at a workshop on Friday, Santosh Misra, Commissioner, TN e-Governance Agency said such a rating mechanism could be spearheaded by a committee of financial institutions and regulators such as RBI and NPCI, among others. \xe2\x80\x9cThe biggest problem any startup faces is credibility. If we have a system where all stakeholders sit together and analyse the startup\xe2\x80\x99s product on various Sindhu.Hariharan parameters, the banks get a comfort level in doing business with the fintech startupsthem,\xe2\x80\x9d Misra told TOI. Such a mechanism could be achieved in the next six months to a year\xe2\x80\x99s time, and can also be scaled globally, he added.

