b'NEW DELHI: Amritsar, Bagdogra and Patna were the fastest growing big Indian airports in terms of seeing passenger number swell in 2018 over the previous year. The Airports Authority of India (AAI) has compiled data for big airports, that handle over 20 lakh passengers a year. Amritsar logged the highest passenger growth with 48.1% increase in flyer number in 2018 over 2017. Bagdogra and Patna were a close number 2 and 3 at 48% and 47.3% growth, respectively.


