b'BENGALURU: Infosys's two controversial acquisitions - Panaya and Skava, which were bought for $340 million - have found no takers. The company had put these two firms on sale, after writing down their value. But now the company appears to be writing off the investment. Beginning 2018, the company started provisioning by way of additional depreciation and amortisation. Currently, the net carrying value of the assets is $206 million.


The two acquisitions have been roiled by controversy almost from the time they were made in 2015. There were charges of excess valuation. There were allegations that some company executives had vested interests in the Panaya acquisition. These were issues that became part of a larger investigation by an international investigating body. That investigation did not find any wrongdoing.


