            \xe2\x80\x9cThe matter will come up before the Chandigarh bench of the National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) on January 23. There was a second bidder in the fray which may now be sounded out. If the second bidder is interested, many things can be sorted out and company will have somebody to run it,\xe2\x80\x9d said Punit Dutt Tyagi, executive partner, Lakshmikumaran & Sridharan. Trouble is, once the top bidder is chosen, the second bidder\xe2\x80\x99s offer is no longer available. So if the second applicant is no longer interested, the whole resolution process will need to be repeated and the current vacuum in Amtek Auto will continue. \xe2\x80\x9cOnce the resolution process is under way, the successful bidder takes over from the RP who had earlier taken over from the company\xe2\x80\x99s promoters,\xe2\x80\x9d said Tyagi. \xe2\x80\x9cToday the old promoters are gone, there is no board, no RP and no new bidder either. There is no management to take the responsibility of running the company, looking into vendors dues, salaries and other statutory requirements and obligations. There is no precedence for this and this vacuum cannot continue,\xe2\x80\x9d he explained.Delhi-based auto component company Amtek Auto\xe2\x80\x99s insolvency resolution process was triggered by Corporation Bank. When the case was taken up by the NCLT, Amtek owed a total of Rs 12,603 crore to various lenders. Liberty House had put in a bid to pay the creditors Rs 3,225 crore and pump in another Rs 500 crore into Amtek Auto. This was approved by the financial creditors in April last year by over 94% vote.However, with Liberty House not paying up citing a mismatch in the Information Memorandum contacting valuation information of Amtek Auto assets, the lenders have now asked that the time Liberty House took in considering the bid be excluded from the 270-day resolution period mandated by the bankruptcy code.\xe2\x80\x9cUnder Section 74 of IBC the NCLT can order action against the promoters of Liberty House, seek damages including the cost of the resolution process,\xe2\x80\x9d said Tyagi. Amtek Auto\xe2\x80\x99s share price on the BSE slid by more than 17% in the last one month from Rs 3.6 per share on December 17 to Rs 2.97 on Monday.'

b'Chennai: The success of co-working coupled with a need to cater to the growing millennial demographic has seen real estate players warm up to the co-living model to monetise their unsold inventory.

Real estate companies TOI spoke to said parts of their inventory are already operating as shared living spaces, and they are in \xe2\x80\x98final stages\xe2\x80\x99 of collaborating with co-living operators to put up unsold inventory with them. Returns on the co-living model typically involve a revenue-share arrangement, and developers report opportunities to earn almost double the yield on a traditional renting model.



