b'NEW DELHI: Trai's Rs 3,050-crore penalty recommendation on Airtel, Vodafone and Idea Cellular over interconnect (IUC) provision to Reliance Jio has not got a green signal from a high-powered committee of the telecom ministry, which has raised questions over the regulator's authority to raise such a financial penalty.


The matter is now expected to be taken up with the inter-ministerial telecom commission, which is the highest decision-making body on telecom matters, sources told TOI.


