Vegetable prices contracted an annual 16.1%, while sugar and confectionary declined 9.2%. Food and beverages contracted 1.5% during the month. Separate data showed wholesale price inflation slowed to an eight-month low in December on the back of easing food, fuel and manufactured product prices.

The annual rate of inflation, based on monthly wholesale price index, stood at 3.8% in December, slower than 4.6% in the previous month and 3.58% during the corresponding month of the previous year. Economists said they expect retail inflation to remain moderate in the months ahead.

