b'NEW DELHI: India will likely be a larger economy than the US by 2030, while China will top the list and Indonesia will figure among the top five, a research report has predicted.


Seven of the top 10 economies in the world by 2030 are likely to be from current emerging markets based on purchasing power parity (PPP) exchange rates and nominal GDP, according to a research report of Standard Chartered.


