b'CHENNAI: Having endured yet another disappointing Ranji campaign, Tamil Nadu will be mere spectators when the quarterfinals commence on Tuesday. But two of their former players \xe2\x80\x94 KB Arun Karthick and R Malolan \xe2\x80\x94 are expected to have key roles for their sides Kerala and Uttarakhand respectively in the last-8 stage. While Arun has 200 runs from 6 games this season, allrounder Malolan \xe2\x80\x94 in his maiden season as a professional \xe2\x80\x94 has managed 107 runs and 16 wickets in 8 outings.


Arun \xe2\x80\x94 who left the TN fold five seasons ago and played for Assam before moving to Kerala in 2017-18 season \xe2\x80\x94 credits the Sachin Baby-led side\xe2\x80\x99s \xe2\x80\x98win at all costs\xe2\x80\x99 attitude as a key reason behind the team\xe2\x80\x99s success. \xe2\x80\x9cKerala as a team has a lot of self-belief. There is a strong bond between the team members and we always aspire to win the matches. Even during the game against Tamil Nadu (at Chepauk that Kerala lost) we could have played for a draw but instead went for the target. It may not have paid off on that occasion, but it has helped us grow a winning mentality,\xe2\x80\x9d Arun told the TOI on Monday. Kerala, who made their maiden knockouts last year, chased down 297 against Himachal in the last league clash to seal their quarters berth where they face Gujarat at Wayanad.


