\xe2\x80\x9cIt comes with a very heavy heart to announce my retirement from Indian national football team. It\xe2\x80\x99s been a very hard decision to take and accept. I love to play more years at my best, but I think it\xe2\x80\x99s the time to step down and give opportunities to youngsters who can perform better,\xe2\x80\x9d said 31-year old Anas in his Instagram post.

\xe2\x80\x9cPlaying for the national team is the top achievement in my career; although the journey was short. Each and every time, I tried to give more than 100 percent for the team. I was so disappointed to pick up an injury in the opening minutes of my final game and it will hurt me forever,\xe2\x80\x9d added Anas.

Anas was a late entrant into the national team as he took almost 11 years to get a national call-up after making his professional debut in 2007 at the age of 20. He quickly made his mark and was one of the pillars of Indian defence under Stephen Constantine as he went on to make 19 first-team appearances for India after making his debut in 2017.

With Constantine deciding to end his coaching reign with India soon after his team\xe2\x80\x99s heart-breaking defeat to Bahrain, one of his favourite ward has also decided to exit the stage. 

\xe2\x80\x9cI just want to say a huge thanks to the coach Stephen Constantine for believing in me and giving me the opportunity and I wish you good luck for the future. Also thanks to all the coaching staffs, teammates, the fans and who all have supported me throughout my journey for the national team. I have been blessed to play for my country, with some of the best players,\xe2\x80\x9d said Anas, who was honoured with AIFF\xe2\x80\x99s best defender award in 2017.

Anas\xe2\x80\x99s career has been hampered by injuries. Last season, the centre-back missed 10 ISL games due to injury, which was the latest in a string of injuries of his career.

\xe2\x80\x9cHe was suffering from various injuries for quite some time. He was very much disappointed to miss out India\xe2\x80\x99s crucial match against Bahrain and the way India went down. Also, he might have thought that he could extend his career a little bit more if he could concentrate on domestic football,\xe2\x80\x9d said former India midfielder NP Pradeep, who has played with Anas earlier in his career.

Mohammed Rafi, who was Anas\xe2\x80\x99s teammate at Kerala Blasters, felt that the centre-back could have played a little more for the national side. 

\xe2\x80\x9cI don\xe2\x80\x99t know what made him take this decision. But I strongly believe that a lot more football is left in him and it is too early for a player like Anas to retire from international football,\xe2\x80\x9d said Rafi.

There are indications that Anas might join ATK on loan for the remainder of ISL season from Kerala Blasters.

'

