b'MUMBAI: As far as the statistics go, Raymond Domenech ranks as the third-longest serving manager of the French national team. Where he stands in the popularity charts, however, is another matter.


Sure, for someone as criticised as Domenech was, the ugly manner in which his six-year stint in charge of Les Bleus ended at the 2010 World Cup did his image no good. Yet, there were many who were reluctant to give the man his due even as he brought the nation to the brink of a second World Cup crown four years prior to the jinxed South African campaign.


