\xe2\x80\x98It was the squad rallying around Zinedine Zidane that propelled France to the 2006 final, not Domenech\xe2\x80\x99s tactical acumen\xe2\x80\x99 has always been the popular belief shared by many in France.

In a candid chat with TOI on Tuesday, the 66-year-old tactician, who was here to attend a round table with key stake holders of Indian football about player development and possible ways for Indian and French football to collaborate, was unflustered on being asked if the lack of recognition of his contribution stung.

It was nothing new in France, he pointed out.

\xe2\x80\x9cNo, because they said the same thing with Aime Jacquet,\xe2\x80\x9d said Domenech, referring to the man who guided France to their maiden World Cup triumph in 1998.

\xe2\x80\x9cEvery time when you have such a player, when you are a coach with a player like Johan Cruyff or (Alfredo) Di Stefano, everybody says the same.

\xe2\x80\x9cBut it was a reality on the pitch when you have players like that. I built the team for Zidane. Like Aime Jacquet in 1998, he built the team to make Zidane the best.

\xe2\x80\x9cEvery time when you have a player of high level, you must make the team for him. You can\xe2\x80\x99t have a problem with him. After that, journalists, we know how you are,\xe2\x80\x9d Domenech added with a wry chuckle, suggesting the French media had a part to play in undermining his role.

The former Lyon manager chronicled his time as head coach of France in a book that was released in 2012 titled Tout Seul, which, in English, means All Alone. With no English translation of it available, however, Domenech was happy to share an anecdote from the build-up to France\xe2\x80\x99s memorable quarterfinal win over a starstudded Brazil that may get many of his critics to alter their dimmed perception of his managerial ability.

\xe2\x80\x9cI remember before the game against Brazil in 2006, we had a discussion about how we will play them. Some players thought we must play with two centre forwards. Everybody was talking. I took the leaders to the side \xe2\x80\x94 (Lilian) Thuram, Zidane, (Thierry) Henry and I said, \xe2\x80\x98I don\xe2\x80\x99t know really for the moment how we will play with them, but during training, we will try two solutions \xe2\x80\x94 a solution with one centre forward and a solution with two centre forwards.\xe2\x80\x99 \xe2\x80\x9cBut I did, on the pitch, what I wanted. (For one half) I put a team with the organisation that I didn\xe2\x80\x99t want, and I put the solution that did not work. The other one, which I wanted, I was sure it worked and they would take. At the end, the players said to me \xe2\x80\x98the second half was much better. We want to play like that\xe2\x80\x99.

\xe2\x80\x9cPerhaps the players think they decided to play like that. That\xe2\x80\x99s not a problem for me. I\xe2\x80\x99m not proud that I tell myself \xe2\x80\x98I decided, I choose\xe2\x80\x99, No. What I wanted is to go to the final,\xe2\x80\x9d said Domenech, stressing on the balancing act he felt was necessary to maintain in order for the team to reach its goal.

\xe2\x80\x9cThat\xe2\x80\x99s management. If I say to Zidane, \xe2\x80\x98we play like that\xe2\x80\x99, and Thierry Henry and Thuram don\xe2\x80\x99t want to, but Zidane wants to, well, we wouldn\xe2\x80\x99t have been in the final.

\xe2\x80\x9cWhen you have great players, you must speak with them. You can\xe2\x80\x99t say \xe2\x80\x98I\xe2\x80\x99m the boss, I decide\xe2\x80\x99. That\xe2\x80\x99s impossible.\xe2\x80\x9d

Attempts to do so, Domenech said, would only result in one winner as he highlighted Jose Mourinho\xe2\x80\x99s much-publicised discord with current France star Paul Pogba at Manchester United as an example.

\xe2\x80\x9cThat\xe2\x80\x99s the problem of Mourinho, he wants to be the leader, even when he has big players like Pogba.

\xe2\x80\x9cPogba, you have to manage him like Zidane,\xe2\x80\x9d said Domenech, who currently serves as President of the National Union of French Coaches.

Having recently met with reigning France manager Didier Deschamps, Domenech shed light on why Pogba was a different player for Les Bleus to the one who had been struggling to deliver under Mourinho.

\xe2\x80\x9cDeschamps said to me, with Pogba, he spends hours and hours speaking with him, to explain what he wants. Pogba needs that, Zidane needs that, all great players need that.

\xe2\x80\x9cThey want to be important, and you have to work with that. If you think you are more important than the biggest player of your team, you\xe2\x80\x99re wrong.\xe2\x80\x9d


'

