b'Chennai: While a steep rise in ownership costs have hurt sales of new cars, SUVs and vans, used vehicles have actually benefited from this. According to organized used car players like Mahindra First Choice Wheels, OLX and Truebil, the sharp increase in cost of ownership that hit new passenger vehicle sales has actually improved the value proposition of used cars prompting a demand shift from new to used vehicles. 

That explains why new passenger vehicle sales are stuttering with less than 5% growth in the April-December period, while used cars and SUVs are vrooming ahead with nearly five to six times that figure.



