            Organised used car marketer Mahindra First Choice Wheels has seen a 25%-30% growth in April-December this year over last year, said Ashutosh Pandey, CEO, Mahindra First Choice Wheels. \xe2\x80\x9cPeople looking to save every penny are finding used options better bargains. If someone wants to buy a Toyota Corolla, he may opt for a used version costing Rs 11-12 lakh rather than a new one costing Rs 20 lakh. Rather than upgrading, customers are shifting from new to used.\xe2\x80\x9d

Also some of the cost bites are less ouch-worthy in used cars because the asset is already depreciated. \xe2\x80\x9cThe 3-year upfront insurance payment has hit new vehicle sales but hurts less in used vehicles as the IDV (insured declared value) of an already depreciated car is less so premium is much lower,\xe2\x80\x9d said Shubh Bansal, co-founder & marketing head of online used car marketplace Truebil. 

Plus, added Pandey, \xe2\x80\x9cused car financing penetration has improved from 15%-20% last year to 25%-30% this year\xe2\x80\x9d even though interest rates are still 200 basis points higher than new cars.

Used cars have also benefited from taxation. Said OLX VP auto Sunny Kataria: \xe2\x80\x9cGST on sale of pre-owned vehicles were taxed at the same rate as new vehicles which was very high at 28% while applicable cess additionally was up to 15%. Due to this effective tax on the sale of pre-owned vehicles was up to 43%. Last year this was lowered to 12%-18% which provided a big fillip to the pre-owned car market.\xe2\x80\x9d


