                      var adContainer = '<div id="div-gpt-ad-1485328452682222244" data-size="fluid" data-adsslot="TOI/TOI_ROS/TOI_ROS_AS/TOI_ROS_AS_Mrec_MID_300" class="webonly alC"></div>';
                      var randomNumber = Math.random();
                      var isIndia = (window.geoinfo && window.geoinfo.CountryCode === 'IN') && (window.location.href.indexOf('outsideindia') === -1 );
                      console.log(isIndia && randomNumber < 0.9 );
                      if(isIndia){
                        // code for showing ctn ad
                         $('#fluid-container').remove();
                         return;
                      }	
                      $('.top2brdiv').remove();
                      $('#fluid-container').append(adContainer);
                    })()



            \xe2\x80\x9cThis has resulted in more trucks chasing lesser cargo. Indulgence in illegal overloading has further flared up and ripped open the entire truck freight market across the country. Consequently, the truck rentals drop is outpacing the drop in diesel price for the last 10 weeks,\xe2\x80\x9d IFTRT stated. Revenues of truckers have shrunk and following this truck sales have begun to slide sharply despite the deep discounts offered by dealers, it said. The truck freight market is in a disarray and stakeholders are waiting for a revival, IFTRT said. Incidentally, the last quarter of the financial year (January-March) typically generates more freight load. Given the overpopulation of medium and heavy trucks in the market, 15%-20% hike in load capacity of heavy vehicles following the revision in safe axle load limits and rampant over-loading for ferrying bulk cargo, truck sales would remain in the negative growth territory, Singh said.'

