            This route has helped corporates float projects larger than their own balance sheet, with higher credit ratings. But it could now be under threat, thanks to IL&FS\xe2\x80\x99 interpretation of an NCLT order that places a moratorium on group companies from repaying debt.

Last week, Jharkhand Road Projects Implementation Company (JRPICL) and West Gujarat Expressway (WGEL) wrote to their trustees, demanding a refund on payments made after October 15, 2018 and intimating that future payments will cease. This is in light of the NCLT-imposed moratorium on IL&FS group companies. 

The surprising part is that both these projects are generating enough cash to make timely payments and continue to enjoy an AA(SO) rating from India Ratings. Their instalment is due on January 21 and January 31 this year, respectively. \xe2\x80\x9cIf JRPICL and WGEL are able to stop the payments, then the ratings on the bonds will have to be downgraded to \xe2\x80\x98IND D\xe2\x80\x99, in line with Sebi\xe2\x80\x99s \xe2\x80\x98one-day, one-rupee\xe2\x80\x99 rule,\xe2\x80\x9d said India Ratings associate director Vishal Kotecha in a note. 

IL&FS SPVs include some large strategic projects, like the Chenani-Nashri Tunnelway (SPV), which is envisaged at a cost of Rs 5,270 crore. \xe2\x80\x9cThe financing document refers to distribution payment conditions, which constrain payments to the sponsor, thereby ring-fencing the SPVs. However, if the project entities decide to interpret the tribunal order and fail to service debt, despite adequate cash availability, in contravention to the spirit of the financing documents, it will result in a multi-notch downgrade,\xe2\x80\x9d said Kotecha.

The development has worried investors in SPVs who now feel that creditors to a stressed sponsor company may now cite this order as a precedent to dip into the cash flows of the SPV. \xe2\x80\x9cIt will be helpful to see a public clarification of the legal position of the SPVs (ring-fenced) executing and operating public-private partnership projects vis-\xc3\xa0-vis a subsidiary, and perhaps even a separate enactment for public infrastructure projects operating on the SPV mechanism,\xe2\x80\x9d said Kotecha.


'

