b'Mumbai: RBI on Wednesday came out with a new policy for overseas borrowings, allowing all eligible entities to raise foreign funding under the automatic route and removing sectoral curbs. All eligible borrowers can now raise external commercial borrowings (ECB) up to $750m per fiscal under the automatic route. tnn 

The "liberalisation/rationalisation" in the new framework ECB and rupee-denominated bonds has been done to further improve the ease of doing business, the central bank said. "Tracks I and II under the existing framework are merged as 'Foreign Currency denominated ECB' and Track III and Rupee Denominated Bonds framework are combined as 'Rupee Denominated ECB' to replace the current four-tiered structure. The framework is instrument-neutral," the RBI said. Track I, II and III denotes amount and maturity of funds raised.



