What is your view of the current state of cricket administration in the country?
Everything is in disarray. There is nobody to take decisions. Rules are being changed in domestic cricket to suit personal needs. There are no committees (disciplinary, technical, etc) in place. What had been a strong administrative policy put in place by BCCI is being destroyed slowly. My question is, how bad were the previous regimes? Administrators in the past helped BCCI reach where it has. Look at how cricket has become a source of livelihood for scores of people.

We worked very hard to promote the game, from all aspects. We were never there for self-publicity. I was hardly seen on public platforms when I served BCCI. We just worked. Now, the difference is that there are individuals who are here to see what they can find for themselves. It\xe2\x80\x99s more about them and not the game. That\xe2\x80\x99s the difference and that\xe2\x80\x99s why there is this mess.


Many feel you were made to look like the person responsible for all the ills\xe2\x80\xa6
I would not like to comment upon a verdict given by the court. But on my part, I\xe2\x80\x99d like to reiterate that I had not done anything wrong. Even during this period (spot-fixing), I stepped aside and asked Mr Dalmiya to look after things. If you ask me, \xe2\x80\x98Were you treated fairly?\xe2\x80\x99, I\xe2\x80\x99d possibly say, \xe2\x80\x98I don\xe2\x80\x99t think so\xe2\x80\x99. But all that is in the past. I haven\xe2\x80\x99t changed my support for this game.


Your son-in-law\xe2\x80\x99s name cropping up in the spot-fixing controversy fuelled this perception\xe2\x80\xa6
In a public position, if a stone is thrown at you, you can\xe2\x80\x99t say, \xe2\x80\x98don\xe2\x80\x99t do that\xe2\x80\x99. People will try to hurt you in different ways. The only point I\xe2\x80\x99d like to emphasize is that I did nothing wrong and I have no rancour.


CSK was banned as a result...
No player made a mistake. The team did not deserve the punishment they got. The simmering anger among the players for being treated like this is what brought about the victory (in 2018). They were determined to prove they were the best.


So you intend to fight your way back\xe2\x80\xa6
Heading the BCCI is a public position and it comes with its share of problems too. But I\xe2\x80\x99ve always been a fighter. I won\xe2\x80\x99t lose and go away.


Shashank Manohar at the ICC and you are at loggerheads\xe2\x80\xa6
I think I clearly misread the man. He has hurt Indian cricket.

