In a statement issued here, SBI said that besides getting the lender\xe2\x80\x99s board clearance, any restructuring plan will need to be approved by RBI, Sebi and possibly the ministry of civil aviation.

Making matters more difficult for the lenders were fresh conditions imposed by Goyal, who said he was willing to invest Rs 700 crore provided his stake does not fall below 25%, while asking for debt relief.

Meanwhile Jet\xe2\x80\x99s minority stakeholders Etihad Airways\xe2\x80\x99 said its investment would be subject to Goyal not holding more than 22% stake. In his letter to SBI, Goyal has warned of \xe2\x80\x9csignificant cash crunch and imminent grounding\xe2\x80\x9d, which the airline is facing. He has also reportedly offered to pledge all his shares if his stake is kept at a minimum 25%.

\xe2\x80\x9cShould this not be possible, then I would not be able to infuse any funds or pledge my shares, unless Sebi accords me me an exemption permitting me to increase my reduced stake (if it is to be below 25%) without triggering the Takeover Code,\xe2\x80\x9d Goyal\xe2\x80\x99s letter said.

Since debt relief typically involves conversion of loans to equity and fresh equity infusion, bankers will find it difficult to arrive at a restructuring plan that all stakeholders agree to. Goyal\xe2\x80\x99s communication to lenders comes a day after his partner Etihad set fresh conditions for picking up stake in the distressed airline. In a communication to SBI, Etihad Group CEO Tony Douglas sought a written assurance from SEBI exempting Etihad from pricing norms and a requirement to make an open offer. He has also called for Goyal reducing his stake. \xe2\x80\x9cWithout this approval we are not willing to invest a single penny further,\xe2\x80\x9d Douglas\xe2\x80\x99s letter said.

Lenders have refused to lobby regulators on behalf of Jet Airways or Etihad on pricing norms for preferential shares but they are still hopeful of a deal between the two partners despite strong posturing by both. Typically, lenders must classify a loan as a nonperforming asset if a loan is in default for 90 days. However, if they initiate a restructuring plan, the asset is treated as a stressed loan and requires provisions to be set aside from profits.

Meanwhile, there was fresh media speculation about Spice-Jet being in talks with Jet Airways to pick up stake. While Jet Airway did not respond to a specific query, a spokesperson for SpiceJet said that the airline had no comments to offer on the reports.

Lenders are unwilling to commit to any relaxation on pricing of preferential shares for any new equity investor. They are also unwilling to provide debt relief without conversion of debt to equity.

'

b'MUMBAI: Reliance Industries (RIL) has reported a 9% rise in profit in the third quarter of fiscal 2019 to Rs 10,251 crore\xe2\x80\x94the first private sector company to cross the Rs 10,000-crore quarterly profit milestone\xe2\x80\x94as it benefited from higher price realizations in its petrochemicals, retail and digital services businesses. The company\xe2\x80\x99s total revenues in the December quarter rose 56% to Rs 1.7 lakh crore compared to Rs 1.1 lakh crore a year ago.


Operating profit in its traditional petrochemicals business, the biggest contributor to RIL\xe2\x80\x99s earnings, increased 43% to Rs 8,221 crore while that of retail and digital services (Reliance Jio) zoomed 211% and 64% to Rs 1,512 crore and Rs 2,362 crore respectively. These numbers together more than made up for the contraction in earnings in its refining business\xe2\x80\x94the second largest contributor to RIL\xe2\x80\x99s profit\xe2\x80\x94and losses in the oil & gas exploration unit.


