b'BENGALURU: India\xe2\x80\x99s mobile internet economy is on fire. The country saw the fastest growth in app downloads among major countries between 2016 and 2018, led by a surge in food delivery and finance. It also saw fastest growth in the hours spent on video-streaming apps.

The latest annual data from App Annie, an independent agency that collates data on apps, shows downloads in India (across Android and iOS) growing by 165% in this period. In China, which accounts for almost 50% of all the downloads in the world, it grew by 70%. Indonesia followed at 55%. In food delivery, India saw a dramatic 900% spike in downloads, way more than any other country.


