b'KOCHI: David Frederick Whatmore loves working with the underdogs. Be it masterminding Sri Lanka\xe2\x80\x99s maiden World Cup triumph in 1996 or taking Bangladesh to their first win in Tests in 2005 or guiding Kerala to their first-ever Ranji Trophy semifinal appearance now, the 64-year old has the ability to take his team to unchartered waters with great success.


None of the above teams were the most supreme in terms of talent, but the Aussie has an uncanny knack of getting the best out of the talent at his disposal.


                    (function(){
                      var adContainer = '<div id="div-gpt-ad-1485328452682222244" data-size="fluid" data-adsslot="TOI/TOI_ROS/TOI_ROS_AS/TOI_ROS_AS_Mrec_MID_300" class="webonly alC"></div>';
