b'CHENNAI: In a match that witnessed seven high-quality goals and its fair share of drama, Chennai City FC (CCFC) showed their class to edge past Aizawl 4-3 at the Nehru Stadium in Coimbatore on Friday and maintain their supremacy at the top of the I-League table. Spaniards Pedro Manzi and Sandro Rodriguez scored a brace each for the hosts that helped CCFC take a runaway lead midway through the second half. Things though got a little tight in injury-time with Aizawl FC scoring two late goals but CCFC did enough to bag all the three points.


