b'MUMBAI: Come Sunday, experienced steeplechaser Sudha Singh, who also runs marathons, will be aiming to match Lalita Babar's record of becoming the best Indian finisher at the Tata Mumbai Marathon on three occasions. Also, she will stay in contention for a place in the Indian squad for the Doha World Championships in September if she finishes the race in under 2 hours 37 minutes.


"My only target is to qualify for the World Championships by clocking 2:37:00," said a confident Sudha on Friday. Nevertheless, looking at the timings - 2:48:32 and 2:39:28 - she clocked in 2018 and 2016, when she emerged the best Indian finisher, it sure is a tough target. "The reason I believe I can do it is because of the form I showed at the Kolkata 25K," she said.


