b'With Brexit, the British chumocrats who drew borders from India to Ireland are getting a taste of their own medicine
Describing Britain\xe2\x80\x99s calamitous exit from its Indian empire in 1947, the novelist Paul Scott wrote that in India the British \xe2\x80\x9ccame to the end of themselves as they were\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x80\x94 that is, to the end of their exalted idea about themselves. Scott was among those shocked by how hastily and ruthlessly the British, who had ruled India for more than a century, condemned it to fragmentation and anarchy; how Louis Mountbatten, accurately described by the right-wing historian Andrew Roberts as a \xe2\x80\x9cmendacious, intellectually limited hustler,\xe2\x80\x9d came to preside, as the last British viceroy of India, over the destiny of some 400 million people.



