Most potential acquirers have indicated that they would offer a lower price, if founders are not part of the deal and management control doesn\xe2\x80\x99t come along. The buyer would then acquire Siddhartha\xe2\x80\x99s stake and mop up some more from the stock markets to trigger an open offer, besides calling shareholders\xe2\x80\x99 meet to rejig the board. \xe2\x80\x9cIf it delivers management rights, the offer price would be significantly higher. It would slightly lag prevailing price otherwise,\xe2\x80\x9d said a person involved with the developments but speaking in private citing confidentiality clauses.

Mindtree shares have perked up in recent days and ended at Rs 889 apiece on Friday, giving the company a market value of over $2 billion.TOIreported on December 17 that Siddhartha\xe2\x80\x99s exit could trigger takeover jitters for Mindtree. Siddhartha did not respond to calls and text messages over the weekend. Mindtree spokesperson said, \xe2\x80\x9cThis is a speculative report. As a matter of policy, the company does not comment on speculation.\xe2\x80\x9d

But founders showed no signs of giving up and reiterated plans to retain control in last week\xe2\x80\x99s investor call following the latest quarterly results. Mindtree, like its bigger peer Infosys, has a tradition of passing the baton to all the founders to steer the company as chief executive. Ravanan, still in his late 40s, would be the last in the line of founders to lead the company.

