            Working through video calls gave this high performer the flexibility to attend to his personal duties as well as keep pace with his work. \xe2\x80\x9cThe move helped him sort things out on the home front. It worked for him and for us as well,\xe2\x80\x9d said a senior executive from the firm, who did not wish to be named. Whether it\xe2\x80\x99s policies around allowing employees to work from home according to their requirements or companies opting for staggered working hours, the factors involved are driven by the various changes taking place in society, largely in metro cities.

To ensure a more even distribution on the local infrastructure \xe2\x80\x94 increasingly distressed in burgeoning cities \xe2\x80\x94 Axis Bank recently introduced staggered work hours for employees at two of its key locations in Mumbai (Worli and Airoli), which house nearly 6,000 employees. In the first month itself, the bank witnessed an even distribution in the number of cars/cabs that entered its premises, said Axis Bank HR head Rajkamal Vempatti. 

\xe2\x80\x9cEarlier, approximately 1,500 vehicles (four-wheelers/two-wheelers) would converge at the two premises between 9:15am and 10:00am. The traffic is now spread more evenly between 7:30am to 10:30am. There is seen to be an increasing trend in the uptake of staggered work hours,\xe2\x80\x9d said Vempatti.

Elaborating on why flexibility at the workplace is becoming more and more important, Deloitte India partner and chief talent officer S V Nathan said, \xe2\x80\x9cThree things are changing at work \xe2\x80\x94 the work, the workforce and the workplace. The way work is delivered, too, is changing. Work happens at any time and at any place. It\xe2\x80\x99s thus important for organisations to recognise these changes. If you don\xe2\x80\x99t take care of your people, somebody else will.\xe2\x80\x9d

The pace of work can be staggered or flexible, depending on the requirement. Nathan said if an organisation is able to address these two, then it can go a long way in upping the happiness quotient of people at work. \xe2\x80\x9cWith a growing number of nuclear families, people struggle to keep pace with a five- or six-day working week. Small tweaks, like allowing somebody to work for less than 40 hours a week, can make a difference to people\xe2\x80\x99s lives and to organisations themselves. We have been experimenting with such initiatives and following the principle of flexibility in spirit,\xe2\x80\x9d said Nathan.

Several companies have eliminated the concept of fixed work hours. At VLCC, all employees across departments and bands can work according to timings most suitable to them and out of any of the VLCC centres convenient to them, said global head of HR operations & people analytics of the company, Pranav Jyoti. \xe2\x80\x9cSalary payouts are not driven by attendance and biometrics, but are driven by key result area and goal sheet,\xe2\x80\x9d said Jyoti. \xe2\x80\x9cOffice infrastructure and facility is an option available for use of employees, but it\xe2\x80\x99s not mandatory to follow daily attendance or timings,\xe2\x80\x9d Jyoti added.


