b'NEW DELHI: The government is ready with rules to lift corporate veil around multi-layered companies. Shareholders and companies with over 10% stake in a company will have to disclose the ultimate beneficiaries of shares, especially overseas owners. 


The revised rules on significant beneficial ownership, which are expected to be notified by the ministry of corporate affairs over the next few days, will provide separate norms for companies where the beneficial owners are Indian companies and those with overseas entities, sources told TOI. 


