b'BENGALURU: Sequoia Capital India, the largest venture capital firm operating in the country, is launching a startup accelerator and incubation programme called Surge where it will pick up 10\xe2\x80\x9320 early stage startups twice every year and invest $1.5 million in each of them at the start of the programme. Sequoia is likely to invest over $100 million over the next 4-5 years in the new initiative, said two people familiar with the development. 


Sequoia\xe2\x80\x99s push, which is perhaps the largest such programme launched in India, is likely to shake-up the sluggish early stage financing market and further spur entrepreneurial activity, according to experts tracking the space. 


