Pliskova will next play US Open champion, Japan\xe2\x80\x99s fourth seed Naomi Osaka, who put out the sixth seed Ukraine\xe2\x80\x99s Elina Svitolina 6-4, 6-1. For most part of the quarterfinal, it looked like a rematch of that controversial New York final of five months ago was on cards \xe2\x80\x93 Osaka versus Williams. Part II. But it wasn\xe2\x80\x99t to be.

Williams, who didn\xe2\x80\x99t call for a trainer after what appeared to be a strain, said her ankle was fine, but added that she wouldn\xe2\x80\x99t know for sure until the next day. \xe2\x80\x9cI hate calling the trainer out. And at that point, I didn\xe2\x80\x99t feel like I needed it or think it would be a big deal. I like to tough it out.\xe2\x80\x9d

She was quick to applaud her conqueror. \xe2\x80\x9cShe played lights out on match point, literally, hitting lines. Just went crazy on match point,\xe2\x80\x9d the American said. \xe2\x80\x9cThere was nothing I did wrong on those match points. I stayed aggressive. She just literally hit the lines on some of them. One she hit an ace, unreturnable serve. Like I literally did everything I could on those match points. I can\xe2\x80\x99t say that I choked on those match points. She literally played her best tennis ever on those shots.\xe2\x80\x9d

The stats, however, told a different story. Pliskova had one winner on match point, the other three were Williams\xe2\x80\x99 forehand errors.

Williams didn\xe2\x80\x99t win a single point on her serve after she hurt her ankle, but refused to blame it for her loss. \xe2\x80\x9cShe started playing really, really good. I don\xe2\x80\x99t think it had anything to do with my ankle. I think she was just nailing and hitting shots. Obviously, I made some mistakes, but she played really well after that.\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x80\x9cI was almost in the locker room, my mind was already there,\xe2\x80\x9d Pliskova told the crowd at the Rod Laver Arena, \xe2\x80\x9cbut now I\xe2\x80\x99m standing here as the winner.\xe2\x80\x9d

Williams, whose movement was hampered after she strained her ankle, said she was willing herself to fightback. \xe2\x80\x9cI\xe2\x80\x99m just trying to win some points, win this game. Then I had a couple more match points on her serve. Naturally, I thought, all right, here we go, you\xe2\x80\x99re going to win one of these. That clearly didn\xe2\x80\x99t happen, but I was just trying at that point,\xe2\x80\x9d she said, adding, \xe2\x80\x9cI don\xe2\x80\x99t think she gave up at all. She didn\xe2\x80\x99t start playing until she was down match point. I think she really gave it her all at that point.\xe2\x80\x9d

Williams chasing a record-equaling 24th Grand Slam title, that will tie her with Margaret Court, said she was looking at winning. \xe2\x80\x9cI\xe2\x80\x99m not going to sit here and lie about that. But it hasn\xe2\x80\x99t happened yet, but I feel like it\xe2\x80\x99s going to happen. Just keep soldiering on, I guess,\xe2\x80\x9d she said.

'

