b'WAYANAD: \xe2\x80\x9cWe were richer for the experience,\xe2\x80\x9d says coach Dav Whatmore when reminded about the thrashing that Kerala got from Vidarbha last year. Vidarbha had won the Ranji Trophy quarterfinal that time at Surat by 412 runs, which remains their biggest victory margin, and went on to create history in the final. 


From Thursday, the two teams will face-off again at Wayanad, this time in the semi-final. The defeat in Surat is the only one Kerala have faced in their six Ranji Trophy encounters against Vidarbha. Prior to last season, Kerala had a clean slate against Vidarbha; they had won twice while three matches ended in draw. Then, the 412-run debacle happened. 


