b'NEW DELHI: In a reprieve to the two-time Commonwealth Games champion, Khumukcham Sanjita Chanu, the International Weightlifting Federation (IWF) on Wednesday revoked her provisional suspension for a failed dope test, paving the way for the Manipuri weightlifter to return to the competitive arena. 


Sanjita, who had returned positive for anabolic steroid \xe2\x80\x98testosterone\xe2\x80\x99 ahead of the World Championship in Anaheim, US in November 2017, has decided to report to the national camp in NIS, Patiala to prepare for the Olympic qualifiers for the 2020 Tokyo Games. In the same championship, her compatriot Mirabai Chanu had clinched a historic gold in the 48kg category. \xe2\x80\x9cI have seen the good news today. I am innocent and I have never taken any banned substance. I am just relieved this is over and I can concentrate on my sport again,\xe2\x80\x9d Chanu told TOI from Imphal.


