b'Coimbatore: Workers of a company facing corporate insolvency resolution process (CIRP) under the \xe2\x80\x98Insolvency and Bankruptcy (I&B) Code (IBC)\xe2\x80\x99 would not be given higher priority over others in claiming pending provident fund (PF) dues. The National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT), Chennai bench, has rejected the claim made by the Regional Provident Fund (PF) Commissioner seeking first priority in recovery of PF dues over all other dues from a company facing corporate insolvency resolution process (CIRP) under IBC.

