Congress was reacting to news reports that the Centre plans to unveil a normal annual budget as against the expected vote on account on February 1. Tewari asked how could a government present a budget for 365 days when it would have barely 56 days left in office till May 26.

\xe2\x80\x9cFrom where does the government derive the locus to present budget for 365 days?\xe2\x80\x9d he remarked, adding that there was a laid down process for the passage of budget which includes vetting by the parliamentary standing committees and passing of the finance bill by parliament.

