b'LONDON: The UK subsidiary of Punjab National Bank (PNB) has lost a Rs 320 crore ($45 million) case in the high court here in which the judge blasted the bank for making a fraudulent misrepresentation claim against nine recipients of its loans that \xe2\x80\x9cwas so abstract it was totally inadequate\xe2\x80\x9d.


Chief Master Marsh ruled that the UK was not the correct jurisdiction for the case, revoked permission to serve the defendants by email and revoked permission for extending the period of service of the claim form, meaning that the stateowned bank can no longer bring any claim against the nine defendants in the UK.


