b'NEW DELHI: The Supreme Court on Friday upheld the validity of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) in its entirety and showered wholesome praise on the NDA government for enacting the code in 2016, by saying it ended \xe2\x80\x9cdefaulters\xe2\x80\x99 paradise\xe2\x80\x9d and allowed the economy regain its rightful position.


After an analysis of benefits accruing from the code in dealing with bankrupt companies, a bench of Justices R F Nariman and Navin Sinha said, \xe2\x80\x9cFigures show that the experiment conducted by enacting the IBC is proving to be largely successful.\xe2\x80\x9d 


