\xe2\x80\x9cIt\xe2\x80\x99s one of the best matches I have ever had on this court, everything worked, everything I imagined before the match I was able to do. It was a perfect match for me, first to last point,\xe2\x80\x9d Djokovic said. \xe2\x80\x9cIt\xe2\x80\x99s a tough one for Lucas, but he had a great tournament. This was his first (Grand Slam) semifinals, so there\xe2\x80\x99s always more weight, more nerves. He\xe2\x80\x99ll get more such matches.\xe2\x80\x9d

Djokovic, who had an elbow surgery 12 months ago, believed he would be back to playing at this level again. \xe2\x80\x9cI thought I\xe2\x80\x99d be here, I have belief and belief always prevails,\xe2\x80\x9d he said.

The Frenchman, who wore his loss better than Tsitsipas on Thursday, said there wasn\xe2\x80\x99t much he could do on the day. \xe2\x80\x9cI was trying to find a solution, but couldn\xe2\x80\x99t find any,\xe2\x80\x9d Pouille, who hadn\xe2\x80\x99t won a match this season coming into the first Grand Slam of the year, said. \xe2\x80\x9cHis first mistake came late in the first set. If I wanted to get close, at least make it 4-all at the end of one set, I had to serve 90 percent or 100 percent first serves. Even with this I was not sure to get close. He just played amazing.\xe2\x80\x9d

\xe2\x80\x9cWhen he\xe2\x80\x99s playing like this he\xe2\x80\x99s the best in the world for sure,\xe2\x80\x9d Pouille said, weighing in on the final. \xe2\x80\x9cWe\xe2\x80\x99ll see on Sunday how he goes, because Rafa looks pretty amazing too. I think they are going to make a great match again. But I think when Djokovic doesn\xe2\x80\x99t make any mistake, he\xe2\x80\x99s moving so well, he\xe2\x80\x99s coming back from defence to offence, he\xe2\x80\x99s playing perfectly good, I think he\xe2\x80\x99s the best player in the world when he\xe2\x80\x99s playing like this.\xe2\x80\x9d

The world No. 1 wrapped up the first set 6-0 in 23 minutes. He had 11 winners and one unforced error, a backhand drop shot that found the bottom of the net. The Serb, who lost in the fourth round to Hyeon Chung last year, outpunched Pouille, who just about managed to get on the scoreboard in the second set.

The Serbian, who came out swinging, wanting to send a message to the Spaniard, lost just six points on his serve in the first two sets. The top seed then broke in the fourth game of the third set and again in the eighth to close out the match.

The last time Djokovic and Nadal clashed at Melbourne Park was seven years ago (2012) in the final, where they played an epic that lasted five hours and 53 minutes. \xe2\x80\x9cThis time, we have the super tie-break (in the fifth set), so I don\xe2\x80\x99t think it will go that far,\xe2\x80\x9d Djokovic said. \xe2\x80\x9cHopefully, the outcome will be the same for me. I would definitely buy a ticket for that match.\xe2\x80\x9d

