b'Remember the TV ads where \xe2\x80\x9cdadaji\xe2\x80\x9d blesses newly married couples, kisses young kids and shakes a leg even as the jingle \xe2\x80\x9casli masala sach sach\xe2\x80\x9d plays in the background? That\xe2\x80\x99s Dharam Pal Gulati, who at 95, is probably the world\xe2\x80\x99s oldest ad star. And that\xe2\x80\x99s not his only claim to fame. Gulati is the owner of the Rs 2,000-crore Mahashaya Di Hatti (MDH) group and has just been conferred the Padma Bhushan for trade and industry.

The phone has not stopped ringing since last night\xe2\x80\x99s announcement but Gulati popularly known as \xe2\x80\x9cMahashaya ji\xe2\x80\x9d with his trademark red turban and white moustache is used to being recognized. And he loves it. \xe2\x80\x9cMain aur koi nasha nahi karta. Mujhe pyaar ka nasha hai (I have no addiction except an addiction to love). I love it when children and young people meet me and take pictures and selfies,\xe2\x80\x9d he says.



