Nadal, shooting for an 18th major title, and a second here at the Rod Laver Arena, that would make him the only man in the Open era to win a second career Slam, said the challenge has always been to adjust his game to his age. \xe2\x80\x9cThat\xe2\x80\x99s what I\xe2\x80\x99ve been doing all my career, adapt my game with the circumstances. That\xe2\x80\x99s why I\xe2\x80\x99m still here competing at a high level. I know during my 16-17 years of playing professional tennis, I\xe2\x80\x99m going to lose things, so I need to add new things,\xe2\x80\x9d Nadal, quick to work the balance, said.

Djokovic, who won their last meeting here, a 5 hour 53-minute epic back in 2012, leads the rivalry 27-25. He also won their last encounter, at Wimbledon in 2018, 10-8 in the fifth set.

The Serb, going for a record seventh crown here, will attempt to match the added miles to the Nadal serve with his own alacrity on the return. A rapier of a shot that has time and again dissected the best of serves. \xe2\x80\x9cHe has improved his serve. He\xe2\x80\x99s backing his first shot up with that great serve, saving energy, and then he can go for more in the return game,\xe2\x80\x9d Djokovic said of the most scrutinized shot here. \xe2\x80\x9cAt the same time it\xe2\x80\x99s quite different playing against me and for me playing against him. It puts more pressure on his serve and my serve, because we both return well.\xe2\x80\x9d


While the second seed has made his serve more of a weapon, he\xe2\x80\x99s also conserving, shortening points and spending less time on the court. Nadal, who didn\xe2\x80\x99t play a competitive match since the US Open, has enjoyed as much success on the shorter rallies (less than four shots) winning 391 of 674 points as with the longer exchanges (nine plus shots), closing out 52 of 82 points. \xe2\x80\x9cI\xe2\x80\x99m not hitting winners every ball. But I play all the shots with a goal. There is no better way to be aggressive than hit every shot with the goal to create damage on the opponent,\xe2\x80\x9d Nadal said. \xe2\x80\x9cToday I can do that damage little bit earlier than before because during this event I have been serving great.\xe2\x80\x9d

While Nadal hasn\xe2\x80\x99t dropped a set in his run to the final, Djokovic, who struggled earlier in the tournament, was all precision in his semifinal against Frenchman Lucas Pouille. \xe2\x80\x9cThis final comes at the right time for both of us,\xe2\x80\x9d the Serb said.

Djokovic, the father of two, who turned his 2018 season around in stunning fashion, winning Wimbledon and the US Open and finishing the year at No.1, said his five-set victory over the Spaniard at the All England Club sealed his comeback from an elbow surgery in January. \xe2\x80\x9cIt allowed me to excel in the months to come after that,\xe2\x80\x9d the superstar Serb said. \xe2\x80\x9cThe Wimbledon semifinals this year, finals of Australian Open 2012, those are the matches where it feels unfair if you have one winner. You want to come out as winner in those matches, but at the same time understanding that you took everything you have out on the court and you left your heart out there, you can be content with that,\xe2\x80\x9d he noted.

\xe2\x80\x9cIt will be a tough one,\xe2\x80\x9d Nadal said. \xe2\x80\x9cI need to be 100 per cent ready for the action. At the same time, it is a motivation for me to play against a player like him in this very important place, against the No. 1 of the world when he\xe2\x80\x99s playing so well. I am excited.\xe2\x80\x9d

If ever Nadal served a verbal warning, this must be it.





