b'MELBOURNE: There were a gamut of emotions on display in the Australian Open women\xe2\x80\x99s final. Shouts of \xe2\x80\x98come on\xe2\x80\x99, clenched fists, screaming winners, nerves, a wobble at the finish line before Naomi Osaka hauled herself across. 


She then went down on the court, head bent, leaning into her racket. Her moment in the middle. Osaka stayed there for a while as the Rod Laver Arena stood to a man applauding. Slowly she rose to her feet, a smile flickering across her face as she took her place among the stars of the game.


