b'Countdown for the most awaited exam for the engineering graduate has begun. With less than 15 days remaining for GATE 2019 exam, aspirants should be aiming to maximise each minute to unlock the GATE of innumerable opportunities. 


GATE exam is scheduled on 2nd, 3rd, 9th, and 10th February and these last few days play a crucial role. Aspirants need to maintain adequate balance between practice of questions and revision, which leads to a good rank. There have been no major changes in GATE pattern since last 3-4 years, which is a positive factor for all appearing candidates. However, one welcoming change is that GATE 2019 examination will be conducted for 24 papers (previously it was 23 papers). The new addition is Statistics and its code is ST.


