b'NEW DELHI: For those familiar with the tech world\xe2\x80\x99s history, it won\xe2\x80\x99t come as a surprise to know that Apple has had a tumultuous past. There was a time \xe2\x80\x93 hard to imagine now \xe2\x80\x93 when Apple products weren\xe2\x80\x99t doing well and there were several mistakes made by the company. However, there was a time when Apple was almost bought over by Sun Microsystems. Yes, Sun Microsystems. Now some of you \xe2\x80\x93 the younger generation \xe2\x80\x93 might wonder Sun Microsystems, who? But there was a time \xe2\x80\x93 in the 90s to be slightly precise \xe2\x80\x93 when Sun Microsystems was a tech behemoth and considered one of the biggest names in the industry.

Almost 22 years ago in 1996, there were a lot of rumours of Sun Microsystems was all set to buy Apple for $3.89 billion, according to a report by CultofMac. Apple back then didn\xe2\x80\x99t have Steve Jobs at the helm of affairs. Jobs had left the company under difficult circumstances a few years back and Apple\xe2\x80\x99s products weren\xe2\x80\x99t really setting the world alight.



