            In fact, this wasn\xe2\x80\x99t the first time when Apple and Sun Microsystems came together. The CultofMac report says that in 1990 it was suggested that both companies came very close to being merged. 

But it wasn\xe2\x80\x99t till 1996 when Apple was on the verge of being taken over by Sun Microsystems. It was rumoured that a deal had been agreed and Scott Mcnealy, COO of Sun Microsystems would head both the companies. However, just before the deal was formalised, Apple announced huge losses amounting upto $69 million which led to the deal falling apart.

A few months later Jobs came back to Apple and the rest, as they say, is history. Jobs scripted an impressive turnaround for Apple and things went kaput for Sun Microsystems as it fell prey to the infamous dot-com bubble. Sun Microsystems was eventually bought over by Oracle in 2009. 

