Admissions in the Journalism and Mass Communication Institutes/Colleges/Universities in the Undergraduate BJMC course, takes place on the basis of your 12th aggregate marks and entrance examination scores. You need to have a minimum of 40% in Class 12th from a recognized education board with one language as a compulsory subject. You can also appear in some most undertaken and prominent BJMC entrance examinations, which includes- Indian Institute of Mass Communication Entrance Exam (IIMC Entrance Exam), Indraprastha University Common Entrance Test for BJMC (IPU CET BJMC), Delhi University Journalism Entrance Exam etc. Some private BJMC Colleges/Institutes even conduct their own Journalism and Mass Communication Entrance Examinations, for admissions into 3 years BJMC course. These entrance examinations contains questions on General English, General Awareness, Mental Ability Reasoning and Media Reasoning. Admissions are done in BJMC Institutes based on their entrance exam scores followed by the personal interview sessions.

If you aspire to become a Reporter, Anchor, Copywriter, Radio Jockey, Content Writer, Brand Manager, PR Professional, Graphic Designer, Producer, Script Writer in your career ahead, then you can check the list of these top Journalism and Mass Communication Institutes/Colleges/Universities according to your preferences.

Below is the list of some top BJMC Institutes/Colleges/Universities in Delhi-NCR region:



International Institute of Mass Media, Delhi
R.K Films and Media Academy, Delhi
ISOMES, Noida
Padarpan Films and Theatre Institute, Delhi
Vivekanand Institute of Journalism and Mass Communication
CG Mantra Digital Media Academy, Noida
Bennett University, Greater Noida
Jagran Institute of Management and Mass Communication, Noida
Noida International University, Noida

