b'NEW DELHI: The Kerala Pareeksha Bhavan is to conduct Kerala Teacher Eligibility Test(KTET) in 2019. The examination is to be conducted in January-February, 2019. As per the latest update from the Examination Commissioner of Kerala, the dates for KTET 2019 January session has been postponed.


KTET 2019 is to be conducted in 4 categories for the school level teachers- KTET 1, KTET 2, KTET 3 and KTET 4. The candidates are informed that the changes in the examination dates has been made for the high school teacher-KTET 3. As per the previous schedule the exam for KTET 3 was to be conducted on February 4, 2019. The new date for KTET 3 exam as per the Kerala Pareeksha Bhavan is February 5, 2019. The examination will conclude on February 6, 2019


